# Engine files that include a shell header, as of today. Each line is a debt,
# not a permission: the gate fails on a NEW edge and fails again on an entry
# here that no longer happens, so a fixed edge cannot quietly stay listed.
#
# search.* -> uci.h        UCIEngine::wdl and format_score on the info line.
#                          Rendering, reached from the search that produces it.
# search.* -> ucioption.h  Search::Worker holds const OptionsMap&; there is no
#                          way to drive a search without a process around it.
# search.* -> timeman.h    the time manager is a search input, zoned to the
#                          shell because the process owns the clock.
# tbprobe.cpp -> ucioption.h   the prober reads SyzygyPath and probe limits.
# types.h -> tune.h        DELIBERATE, and the only entry here that is not debt.
#                          Placed after types.h's own #endif so the SPSA macros
#                          are visible anywhere types.h reaches. Removing it
#                          would make every future tuning run add an include
#                          first. See docs/00-architecture.md.
search.cpp -> timeman.h
search.cpp -> uci.h
search.cpp -> ucioption.h
search.h -> timeman.h
tbprobe.cpp -> ucioption.h
types.h -> tune.h
